From 089307b70f654265c8b92b09148a07f91e147063 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:53:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 236/294] gallium/pvr: two-geometry-submission experiment;
 kernel module gets the upstream paired-job fixes

Round-23 experiment: queueing two geometry jobs back to back (PVR_PROBE_QUEUE_TWO_GEOM) still hangs
(one "Kick TA" with First/Last kick:0, then DM2 timeout), so the firmware is not merely dropping a
context's first TA kick.

Separately: the custom powervr kernel module predates the upstream March-2026 drm/imagination job
submission fixes (it still had pvr_queue_get_paired_frag_job_dep(queue, job)). Backported the two
stable fixes to it:
- "Count paired job fence as dependency in prepare_job()" (9cd74f935306): a fence between paired jobs
  is not UFO-backed until both are submitted, so it must be counted manually when checking CCCB space;
- "Fit paired fragment job in the correct CCCB" (4baf9e70cb75): the paired fragment job's done fence
  and CCCB-space check must use the fragment queue, not the geometry queue.
The patched module builds, the open Vulkan driver still reports PASS, and the native probe's TA stall
is unchanged. Patch kept as open-driver-perf/captures/pvr_queue-r23-backport.diff; the module can be
rebuilt from the kernel-src/powervr worktree.

Verification: probe ALL PASS under the shim.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
index acb12f83..af8f9db7 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
@@ -1301,7 +1301,18 @@ real_job_done:
                          PRIx64 "\n", (unsigned)g_fs_pds_base_offset, rbctaddr);
                }
 
-               if (getenv("PVR_PROBE_GEOM_ONLY")) {
+               if (getenv("PVR_PROBE_QUEUE_TWO_GEOM")) {
+                  /* Queue two geometry jobs back to back before the first one times out: if the
+                   * firmware drops a context's first TA kick, the second one may start. */
+                  const bool s1 = pvr_job_submit(vm, gpu_ctx.handle, DRM_PVR_JOB_TYPE_GEOMETRY,
+                                                 gstream, glen, dset_handle, 0);
+                  const bool s2 = pvr_job_submit(vm, gpu_ctx.handle, DRM_PVR_JOB_TYPE_GEOMETRY,
+                                                 gstream, glen, dset_handle, 0);
+
+                  printf("hwrt:          queued two geometry jobs: submit1=%d submit2=%d\n",
+                         s1, s2);
+                  usleep(500000);
+               } else if (getenv("PVR_PROBE_GEOM_ONLY")) {
                   const bool gdone = pvr_job_submit_geom_sync(vm, gpu_ctx.handle, gstream, glen,
                                                               dset_handle, 0, 2000);
 
